#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:49
msgid "Duplicate a template"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:50
msgid "Creates an isolated working copy of a Builderius template from its saved state: the module tree, entity CSS, entity-scoped data variables and JS snippets all ride along in the copied config. The copy is created DISABLED and without apply rules by default so it can never shadow the original on the front end — pass enabled: true and copy_apply_rules: true only when a live twin is genuinely wanted. Page-bound templates are duplicated as regular templates (a WordPress page can only bind one page template); hook templates keep their hook wiring. The copy starts a fresh commit history."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:57
msgid "Source template post ID or slug."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:61
#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:120
msgid "Title for the copy. Defaults to \"<source title> copy\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:65
#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:124
msgid "Slug for the copy. Defaults to WordPress' unique slug for the title."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:70
msgid "Enable the copy immediately. Default false: a duplicate that is live from birth can conflict with the original."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:75
msgid "Copy the source's apply rules onto the duplicate. Default false so the copy applies nowhere until deliberately targeted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:86
msgid "The duplicate's summary (id, slug, title, enabled, type, apply_rules, branch, commit)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:90
msgid "The source template (id, slug) and the commit the content was copied from."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:108
msgid "Duplicate a component"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:109
msgid "Creates a copy of a Builderius component definition from its saved state: the internal module tree, declared properties (and their derived props variable), entity CSS and entity-scoped data variables all ride along. The copy gets a fresh slug and commit history; existing instances keep pointing at the source component. Use this to fork a shared component before an experiment instead of editing the shared original in place."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:116
msgid "Source component post ID or slug."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:135
msgid "The duplicate's summary (id, slug, title, props, branch, commit)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:139
msgid "The source component (id, slug) and the commit the content was copied from."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:153
msgid "List global settings sets"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:154
msgid "Enumerates the site's Builderius global settings sets — the entities that carry the framework CSS, global data variables and global JS snippets. Most sites have exactly one; when several exist, the global CSS and data-variable abilities need a settings_set reference, and this ability is how an agent discovers the right one. Each row reports the set's identity, saved commit (for the expected_commit save flow), stylesheet size, named CSS blocks, and how many global data variables and JS snippets it holds."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:166
msgid "Per set: id, slug, title, technology, branch_id, commit_name, css_length, css_blocks, data_variables, js_snippets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:180
#: includes/features.php:1006
msgid "Validate a JS snippet"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:181
msgid "Structurally validates JavaScript before it is saved with dbe/manage-js-snippet: unbalanced brackets/braces/parentheses, unterminated strings, template literals, comments and regular expressions, and stray HTML are reported with line numbers. This is a structural scan, not a full ECMAScript parse — code that passes can still contain runtime or semantic errors, so treat a pass as \"safe to save\", not \"proven correct\". Nothing is saved or executed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:188
msgid "The JavaScript source to check."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:200
msgid "Structural problems found, each with a message and line number."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:205
msgid "The level of validation performed (structural)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:218
msgid "Manage an element's rendering conditions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:219
msgid "Reads, sets or clears one element's rendering (visibility) conditions in the saved state — the setting dbe/apply-subtree-html preserves through data-dbe-id markers but cannot express in HTML. Conditions are OR-of-AND groups: pass groups as an array of arrays, each inner array a set of AND-ed rules { name, operator, value } and the outer array OR-ed — e.g. [[{\"name\":\"user_logged_in\",\"operator\":\"is\",\"value\":\"true\"}]] shows the element to logged-in users only. Rule names and operators are validated against Builderius' installed rendering-condition registry (post_type, user_role, url_parameter, is_front_page, dynamic_data, expression, …). Conditions that read the wp system variable (post_type, post_meta, user_role, …) need matching fields in the wp query — the result warns when they look absent, because the builder maintains those automatically and this channel cannot; always prove the element with dbe/check-rendered-output afterwards. Alternatively pass expression for a raw Twig-style condition string. Use action: get first to read the current shape; set replaces the whole condition; clear removes it (the element always renders)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:226
#: includes/abilities/verification.php:493
msgid "Template or component post ID or slug."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:232
#: includes/abilities/verification.php:499
msgid "Entity type of the template reference."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:236
msgid "The element's module ID (find it with dbe/get-tree-outline)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:241
msgid "get reads, set replaces, clear removes the condition."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:245
msgid "For set: OR-ed groups, each an array of AND-ed rules { name, operator, value }. Omit value only for is_empty/is_not_empty operators."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:254
msgid "The comparison value. key_value widgets (post_meta, user_meta, url_parameter, cookie) take \"key:value\" strings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:264
msgid "For set: a raw condition expression string instead of groups (stored verbatim, evaluated by Builderius' expression engine)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:269
msgid "Preview the condition value that WOULD be saved without committing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:273
msgid "The active commit name from the preceding read. Required when saving."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:278
#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:363
msgid "Explicitly override a dirty Builderius-tab conflict."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:289
msgid "The condition value (current for get, resulting for set/clear)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:309
msgid "Manage a global settings set"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:310
msgid "Reads or updates the global settings set's non-CSS settings: the responsive strategy (desktop-first/mobile-first), the named breakpoints behind @media (--tablet)-style queries, and the font declarations. Builderius creates exactly one set per technology automatically, so there is no create or delete — use dbe/list-settings-sets to discover the sets and dbe/get-global-css / dbe/patch-global-css for the stylesheet itself. Changing breakpoints affects EVERY template's responsive CSS; changing the responsive strategy flips which direction the breakpoint media queries cascade — treat both as site-wide design decisions, read first with action: get, and save with the expected_commit flow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:317
#: includes/abilities.php:131
msgid "Global settings set post ID or slug. Omit when the site has one (the usual case)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:322
msgid "get reads the settings; update writes the passed fields as a new commit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:327
msgid "For update: the responsive strategy."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:331
msgid "For update: the COMPLETE breakpoints list, replacing the current one. Each: { name: \"--tablet\", label, width, width_builder?, icon?, deletable? }."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:348
msgid "For update: the COMPLETE font declarations list, replacing the current one. Each: { type, content }."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:354
msgid "Preview the resulting settings without committing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:358
msgid "The active commit name from the preceding get. Required when saving."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:374
msgid "Identity: id, slug, title, technology."
msgstr ""

